/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Question 1 -  What are the key steps involved in data analysis, and why is each step important?)
/E (Question 1 -  What are the key steps involved in data analysis, and why is each step important?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Appropriate Answer - )
/E (Appropriate Answer - )
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Data analysis is a structured process that transforms raw data into meaningful insights for informed decision-making. It begins with data collection, where reliable sources ensure the accuracy of the dataset. Next comes data cleaning, which addresses inconsistencies, missing values, and duplicates to improve data quality. Data exploration follows, allowing analysts to identify patterns, trends, and relationships through statistical summaries and visualizations. Data visualization further simplifies complex information by presenting it in charts, graphs, and dashboards. Ultimately, the goal is drawing insights and making decisions based on the analyzed data, enabling businesses to take strategic actions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 121 0 R
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
