151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Yes! Data cleaning is all about making the dataset usable by fixing errors, handling missing values, and ensuring consistency. For example, if a dataset contains duplicate entries or incorrect date formats, cleaning fixes these issues.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (On the other hand, data exploration is about understanding the dataset. It involves summarizing, finding patterns, and detecting anomalies. I usually generate descriptive statistics and create visualizations like histograms and scatter plots to get a sense of the data.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
