160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Visualization plays a key role in making data insights clearer. Bar charts are ideal for comparing categories, such as sales by product. Line graphs are useful for showing trends over time, like stock prices. Pie charts work well for displaying proportions, though they should be used cautiously. Scatter plots are effective for identifying relationships between two variables, such as age versus income. Heatmaps help spot patterns in large datasets, like customer behavior across different regions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
