184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Certainly! A real-world example I encountered involved a retail company that failed to clean duplicate transactions from their dataset. As a result, the company mistakenly overestimated their total sales by 20%. This led them to order excess stock, resulting in overstocking issues. Once I cleaned the data, eliminating duplicates, the company was able to align their stock levels with actual demand and avoid costly over-purchasing.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
