188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (During data exploration, I typically use descriptive statistics, such as mean, median, mode, and standard deviation, to summarize the data. I also conduct correlation analysis to identify relationships between variables. This helps in understanding whether one variable is dependent on another. Additionally, hypothesis testing helps in determining if observed patterns are statistically significant. For example, while working on a customer churn analysis project, I used correlation analysis to identify factors like customer service interactions and product usage frequency, which were significant predictors of churn.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
