<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Correlation analysis is crucial in EDA because it helps uncover relationships between variables. By calculating correlation coefficients, I can identify how strongly two variables are related. This is particularly useful in understanding whether changes in one variable can predict changes in another. For example, when analyzing marketing data for a company, I used correlation analysis to demonstrate that higher advertising spend was strongly correlated with increased sales, which provided the team with actionable insights for future budgeting.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
