>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Appropriate Answer - )
/E (Appropriate Answer - )
/Alt ()
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Big data refers to extremely large datasets that cannot be processed efficiently using traditional tools. These datasets often involve high volume, velocity, and variety, which require specialized technologies and frameworks like Hadoop, Spark, and NoSQL databases to handle. Unlike traditional data analysis, where data can be processed on a single machine, big data requires distributed computing and advanced techniques to process, analyze, and store the data. In a project analyzing global web traffic, I worked with large-scale data that required Spark for distributed processing to gain insights into user behavior.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
